title: 'Anthropic, Claude Code best practices (2026): say what done looks like, give a check to run, ask for evidence, and review in a fresh context against the spec, skipping style.'
pid: 265a0f2b-0c0e-4fb5-9c74-accfce849a78
body: |2-
  https://code.claude.com/docs/en/best-practices
  A spec written first, then built in a fresh session, gives a clean
  context and a written definition of done. A reviewer that never saw
  the reasoning is not swayed by it; delegating the same task gives
  no better answer, but a fresh reviewer does help. "A reviewer
  that's asked to find problems will always find something." Before
  leaving work unattended: does it know what done is, can it check
  itself, what may it touch, what stops it, who signs off.
